At Home Project: As part of the interview process, we would like you to complete a brief project before your in-person technical interview. Once you have completed the project, please send it to me before your scheduled interview time and I will forward it along to the hiring team. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to reach out. I will follow up with you by phone to coordinate the in-person interview after you have submitted the project.

 Project Overview

Please build a simple web-accessible application that addresses a common organizational challenge. Examples could include task tracking, help desk requests, asset inventory, event registration, volunteer scheduling, meeting coordination, or another practical workplace need.

This project is intended to take no more than one hour. We are not expecting a polished or production-ready application. The goal is to understand how you approach problem solving, structure an application, make technical decisions, and communicate tradeoffs.

Project Requirements

Your application should:

·         Address a clear organizational challenge

·         Be available through a web-accessible URL

·         Include a user-facing interface

·         Include a supporting service or data layer

·         Allow the user to view, create, update, or manage information in some way

Free-tier hosting and simple data storage are acceptable.

Interview Discussion

During the in-person technical interview, you will be asked to walk through what you built. Please be prepared to discuss:

·         The problem you chose to solve

·         How the application works

·         The structure of the user-facing portion of the application

·         The structure of the supporting service or data layer

·         How the application was deployed

·         What decisions you made due to the one-hour time constraint

·         What you would improve if you had more time

What We Are Evaluating

We are primarily interested in your:

·         Problem-solving approach

·         Technical judgment

·         Ability to deliver a working solution within constraints

·         Communication of design decisions and tradeoffs

·         Understanding of how the application could be improved or scaled

**Please bring the web-accessible URL and be ready to demonstrate the application during your interview.**

Please be prepared for a professional interview. It is recommended that you research the company and have a few questions prepared about the organization and/or the position.